						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <div class="scp-image-block block-center" style="width:100%;"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/cack-hub/cack_hard_poster.png" style="width:100%;" alt="cack_hard_poster.png" class="image" /> <div class="scp-image-caption" style="width:100%;"> <p>Bitchin poster made by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wydness" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4862958&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609165866" alt="Wydness" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4862958)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wydness" >Wydness</a></span></p> </div> </div> <br /> <span style="color: white">looking for pattern screamers, are we? Fuck off, pal.</span> <div style="Border:solid 1px #000000; padding:7px; margin-bottom: 10px;"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <h1><span><span style="text-decoration: underline;">What's this?</span></span></h1> </div> <p>The cack hard cinematic universe is home to a bunch of dumb stupid stuff, mostly weird crack fiction. Cack fiction, if you will. This is a world where things always take a turn for the stupid, farcical, and idiotic. This isn't a canon, but simply a hub to host crackfiction too stupid for LolFoundation.</p> <p>Hidden in this collapsible are the general 'rules' which we adhere to when writing within the cack hard cinematic universe. If for whatever reason you want to write crack.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <ul> <li>No one is good at their job unless the plot demands it.</li> <li>Researcher Zyn Kiryu is the only person who is good at her job regardless of the situation.</li> <li>If anyone has to suffer, it's Mr. Fish.</li> <li>049 and Spanko are best buds. No exceptions!</li> <li>'Cack Hard' installments must be a movie of some sort. Continuity is for suckers!</li> <li>Bottledick is canon.</li> <li>The Foundation is less of a jail and more of a hotel.</li> <li>Bottledick is not canon.</li> <li>SCP-055 is a sphere.</li> <li>Dr. Cimmerian sent 650 million emails and crashed scipnet servers for a week.</li> <li>Site-19 has an on-site burger king.</li> <li>WWS is engaged in a bloody war with the Shark Punching Center.</li> <li>Dr. Hamm and SCP-049 are 049-J's fathers.</li> <li>fuck you.</li> <li>If you write in the cack hard cinematic universe, just set this page as your content's parent page.</li> <li>Mixing canons and doing things that don't make any logical sense is not only allowed but encouraged.</li> <li>have fun, damn it. <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><em>this is not a canon</em></span></strong>, more like a loose continuity of crack fiction that is all about writing the stupidest crap you can think of.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span> <div style="Border:solid 1px #000000; padding:7px; margin-bottom: 10px;"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <h1><span><span style="text-decoration: underline;">crack fic? More like cack fic!</span></span></h1> <p>Home to shameful crack fiction which truly, bluely should not have seen the light of day!<br /> Includes such bar-lowering classics as:</p> </div> <br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>SCP</th> <th>Name</th> <th>Author</th> </tr> <tr> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3472-j">SCP-3472-J</a></td> <td>In time, you will come to hate <span style="color: blue">me</span>.</td> <td><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a hre